1
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:10,837
On every shift, technicians check equipment in plant rooms and basements.

2
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:14,611
Down there, there is often no signal.

3
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:18,330
Rounds brings AI to these inspections.

4
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:23,658
But approved rules always decide what is safe.

5
00:00:24,558 --> 00:00:31,398
A supervisor starts with the equipment manual. This one is fictional.

6
00:00:32,368 --> 00:00:38,563
Firebase AI Logic sends it to Gemini, in the cloud.

7
00:00:39,758 --> 00:00:43,018
Gemini turns it into a procedure pack,

8
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:48,240
with clear limits and a short card for each step.

9
00:00:49,728 --> 00:00:56,304
Every limit must quote the manual exactly. The app checks each quote.

10
00:00:57,018 --> 00:01:04,369
Here, Gemini paraphrased a safety line, so the supervisor excludes it.

11
00:01:06,028 --> 00:01:10,049
Only approved items reach technicians.

12
00:01:10,968 --> 00:01:17,147
The technician starts the round. The pack is saved on the device.

13
00:01:17,548 --> 00:01:20,470
Now the connection drops.

14
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:25,278
The technician notes a faint rattle near the pump.

15
00:01:26,568 --> 00:01:28,818
This is hybrid inference.

16
00:01:28,818 --> 00:01:38,532
The same Firebase AI Logic call now runs Gemini Nano, on the device, offline.

17
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:44,370
Next, an abnormal reading: eighty-two degrees.

18
00:01:44,542 --> 00:01:47,682
No AI judges this number.

19
00:01:47,682 --> 00:01:57,015
A rule compares it with the approved limit, quotes the manual, and shows the approved escalation.

20
00:01:57,065 --> 00:02:01,292
This check also failed on an earlier shift.

21
00:02:02,532 --> 00:02:08,267
Vibration is also high, with a squeal near the bearing.

22
00:02:09,932 --> 00:02:11,822
For a cloud review,

23
00:02:11,822 --> 00:02:17,477
the technician sees exactly what will be sent, and agrees.

24
00:02:19,532 --> 00:02:23,592
Offline, the request waits on the device.

25
00:02:24,532 --> 00:02:30,232
When the connection returns, Gemini in the cloud reviews it,

26
00:02:30,232 --> 00:02:33,420
with the manual and the history.

27
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:39,090
At the end, the device drafts the shift handover,

28
00:02:39,090 --> 00:02:42,555
based on the recorded readings.

29
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:47,010
With Rounds, the cloud prepares the knowledge,

30
00:02:47,010 --> 00:02:53,894
the device helps offline, and approved rules decide what is safe.

